{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quadratic trinomial factorization quadratic trinomial factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md","fileName":"Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quadratic Trinomial Factorization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Factoring and Algebraic Identities]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Binomial","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quadratic trinomial factorization quadratic trinomial factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md","fileName":"Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quadratic Trinomial Factorization","heading":"Quadratic Trinomial Factorization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Quadratic trinomial factorization rewrites (ax^2+bx+c) as a product of two [[Binomial]]s when such factors exist. In the monic case,\n\n$$x^2+bx+c=(x+p)(x+q),$$\n\nso the needed numbers satisfy (p+q=b) and (pq=c). For (x^2+5x+6), the numbers are (2) and (3), giving ((x+2)(x+3)).\n\nWhen (a\\neq1), possible factor pairs of both (a) and (c) must be considered. Expansion verifies the chosen factorization.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Binomial","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quadratic Trinomial Factorization.md: